- **Extract Subtitles from Videos:** You can now extract built-in subtitles directly from video files in both Normal and Batch modes. In Normal mode, a "Use embedded subtitle" button appears in the Input Subtitle box when a video is loaded. In Batch mode, right-click a video and choose "Use embedded subtitles" to pick and extract multiple tracks at once. Extracted files are saved next to the video, and a new setting (enabled by default) syncs them against the video's audio. Fixes issue [#73](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/issues/73) by @ElimGarak72.
- **Better Subtitle Encoding & UTF-8 with BOM Default:** Changed the default output format to `UTF-8 with BOM (Recommended)` so synced subtitles display special characters properly in more video players. Also improved automatic text encoding detection for different languages and prevented characters from turning into `?` when saving. Fixes issue [#106](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/issues/106) by @CeoAnonymouse.
- **Portable Mode:** Added a "Portable mode" option in Settings for standalone builds (Windows ZIP, Linux `.tar.gz` / AppImage, and writable macOS `.app` bundles). When turned on, AutoSubSync saves your settings, logs, databases, and downloaded tools in an `AutoSubSync_data` folder next to the app instead of your system folders, and safely moves your existing data over. Fixes issue [#76](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/issues/76) by @macronimus.
- **Always on Top:** Added an "Always on top" option in Settings so you can keep the AutoSubSync window above other windows. Works on Windows, macOS, and Linux (X11, KDE Wayland, and Sway). Fixes issue [#88](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/issues/88) by @Apollyonn.
- **Better PGS (Blu-ray) Subtitle Support:** Enabled built-in PGS subtitle support in `ffsubsync` by default, and allowed `alass` to automatically use a video's built-in PGS subtitles as a timing reference when no text subtitle track is found. Fixes issue [#10](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/issues/10) by @babywin.
- **Smoother Progress Bar & Live Logs:** The progress bar now moves smoothly from 0% to 100% for each sync instead of jumping back to 0% between steps. You can also watch subtitle extraction progress live in the log window and cancel it right away, with cleaner, less cluttered progress lines.
- **LAPSE Speech Filter & Track Options:** Added an optional "Whisper speech filter" in LAPSE's Other options (off by default) that downloads the needed files automatically if you turn it on. Also added a `--sub-track` option for LAPSE, removed the old `--full-scan` option, and made several option tooltips clearer.
- **LAPSE Cache Cleanup:** Added "Clear Lapse cache" and "Open logs directory" buttons in LAPSE's Other options, plus a checkbox in "Clear all logs" if you want to clear LAPSE's cache files at the same time.
- **Safer Downloads with Progress:** Added 0–100% progress bars when downloading FFmpeg, LAPSE, or Whisper, and made sure incomplete or interrupted downloads don't leave broken files behind.
- **WebVTT Short Timestamp Fix:** Fixed shifting and converting WebVTT (`.vtt`) subtitles that don't include hours in their timestamps (such as `01:23.456`). Contributed by @jayhemnani9910 in PR [#105](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/pull/105).
- **Batch Auto-Pairing Fix:** Fixed batch auto-pairing so episode numbers at the end of filenames (like `01` or `02`) aren't mistaken for language codes. Contributed by @jayhemnani9910 in PR [#104](https://github.com/denizsafak/AutoSubSync/pull/104).
